  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 7 is a fog-of-war maze with one target at (29,50), requiring internal tuple (shape=0,color=3,rotation=2). The 42-unit counter drains by 2 per attempted movement, including blocked wall moves, while the moving control freezes on blocked moves. Six reset rings were mapped; five were used live and each restored the counter to 42. Three directional pusher/launcher objects partition the maze: the upper pusher carries the player down into an otherwise isolated right corridor, a vertical pusher can eject the player upward, and the lower horizontal pusher returns the player left. Rotation is controlled by a pinwheel moving vertically at x=54 between y=5 and y=30; following it upward caused two consecutive live matches, advancing rotation 0->1->2. Color and shape are static controls at (9,40) and (19,40), respectively.",
  "narrative": "Resolved the required level-6 replay plan from results/outer_loop_codex_ls20_probe_round8_20260712.json, replayed all 573 labels from a fresh env.reset(), and confirmed frame_level(frame) == 6 with state NOT_FINISHED. Fresh L7 exploration used compact 64x64 frame diffs, object/component dumps, internal tuple/counter snapshots, and a continuously updated /tmp/codex55_ls20_candidate.json checkpoint. The first route mapped the fogged maze, confirmed the 2-unit movement cost, used the upward vertical pusher, collected the upper reset ring, then used the downward pusher to enter the isolated right corridor. Synchronizing with the vertical moving rotation control advanced rotation to 2; the lower-right ring sustained the route, and the horizontal pusher returned the player to the left maze. After several honestly retained blocked scouting moves, the route used the lower-left, top-left, and center rings to cycle color to 3 and shape from 1 through five entries to 0 without exhausting the counter. Six final downward moves entered the sole target with tuple (0,3,2); action 672 returned frame_level 7 and GameState.WIN. The full action_sequence includes the independently verified 573-label prefix and every L7 scouting/solving action. A separate post-win fresh-reset reproduction would require 672 additional env.step calls, but only 278 remained under the 950-call cap, so reproduction_verified is false.",
  "gotchas": [
    "L7 enables fog of war, so distant targets, controls, rings, and corridor geometry are not simultaneously visible; compact component and state dumps were needed while moving.",
    "The counter still starts at 42 but L7 drains 2 units per attempted directional action. Blocked wall moves also drain 2 even though player position and the moving pinwheel phase freeze.",
    "The three directional pushers are forced one-way transports, not tuple controls: entering the upper pusher from below sent the player from (39,25) to (39,40), entering the vertical pusher from above sent (34,25) to (34,10), and entering the lower pusher from below sent (39,35) to (29,30).",
    "The right-hand rotation corridor is unreachable by ordinary walking; the upper downward pusher is the required bridge into it, and the lower horizontal pusher is the return path.",
    "The rotation control moves before collision resolution on each valid action. Its phase must be synchronized: from player (54,35) with the pinwheel approaching y=30, two upward moves matched it at y=30 and y=25 and advanced rotation twice.",
    "Shape starts at 1 and the target requires 0, so the static shape control must be entered five times modulo 6. Color starts at 0 and requires three entries modulo 4.",
    "Reset rings can be used on the action that would otherwise exhaust the counter; the lower-left and top-left rings were deliberately reached with 2 units remaining.",
    "The live win is one continuous fresh-start sequence, but a second full replay did not fit within the global 950-step budget."
  ],
